OL,3,GNEWSAResidents report Bayeux Tapestry
OL,4,Aticket issues
OL,5,
OL,6,FResidents in and around Hastings who
OL,7,Fhad been assured of tickets to see the
OL,8,FBayeux Tapestry say they have had
OL,9,F"considerable difficulty" obtaining the
OL,10,Ftickets.
OL,12,FThe British Museum said that while
OL,13,Fresidents were offered the chance to
OL,14,Fsecure tickets before wider release,
OL,15,Fthese were on a "first come, first
OL,16,Fserved basis".
OL,18,FHastings and Rye MP Helena Dollimore
OL,19,Ftold BBC Radio Sussex that the process
OL,20,Fhas been "shambolic" and that the
OL,21,FBritish Museum should put aside a batch
OL,22,Fof tickets for locals.
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,330,320,200,140,0,100
